<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Czechoslovakia splits peacefully into two states</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dissolution-of-czechoslovakia">Velvet Divorce</a>', <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> dissolved by agreement into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a>. The separation was negotiated by politicians without a referendum and passed without violence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/moscow" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moscow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-3">3 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Bush and Yeltsin sign the START II arms treaty</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, George H. W. Bush and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-yeltsin">Boris Yeltsin</a> agreed to cut their strategic nuclear arsenals by about two-thirds and ban multiple-warhead land-based missiles. The treaty never fully entered into force.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-26">26 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Truck bomb explodes beneath the World Trade Center</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Islamist militants detonated a bomb in the North Tower's underground car park, killing six people and injuring more than 1,000. The towers survived but were destroyed in the attacks of 2001.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-28">28 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Federal raid on the Branch Davidians begins the Waco siege</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A gun battle at the compound near Waco, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>, killed four federal agents and six Branch Davidians. The 51-day siege ended on 19 April in a fire that killed 76 people, including children.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-13">13 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Rabin and Arafat shake hands on the Oslo Accords</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Israel and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine-liberation-organization">PLO</a> signed the Declaration of Principles at the White House, with a historic handshake between Yitzhak Rabin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yasser-arafat">Yasser Arafat</a>. The deal created Palestinian self-rule, but lasting peace proved elusive.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-1">1 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Maastricht Treaty creates the European Union</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maastricht-treaty">Treaty on European Union</a> came into force, establishing the EU alongside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-communities">European Communities</a>. It introduced EU citizenship and set the path to economic and monetary union and the euro.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/dissolution-of-czechoslovakia">Dissolution of Czechoslovakia</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The dissolution of Czechoslovakia, known as the Velvet Divorce, divided the federation into the Czech Republic and Slovakia on 1 January 1993.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mogadishu-1993" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-mogadishu-1993.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mogadishu-1993">Battle of Mogadishu (1993)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Mogadishu was fought on 3–4 October 1993 in the Somali capital, when US special forces trying to capture lieutenants of the warlord Mohamed Farrah Aidid were trapped after two Black Hawk helicopters were shot down.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/multi-party-negotiating-forum">Multi-Party Negotiating Forum</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Multi-Party Negotiating Forum was the body that negotiated the end of apartheid in South Africa in 1993, after the breakdown of CODESA.</p></div></li></ol></section>
